  "content": {
    "text": "What to know about Cursor, the AI coding startup SpaceX is buying for $60 billion\nNewly public SpaceX is taking advantage of a previous agreement that gave it the option to acquire Cursor, whose engineers have already been working closely with the company\nSpaceX is buying a highflying, fast-growing artificial-intelligence startup as it seeks to make its Grok model more competitive.\nOn Tuesday, as SpaceX’s stock SPCX boomed, the company said it would acquire the parent company of the AI coding startup Cursor for $60 billion. The transaction is expected to close by the end of August, according to the companies.",
    "text_blocks": [
      "What to know about Cursor, the AI coding startup SpaceX is buying for $60 billion",
      "Newly public SpaceX is taking advantage of a previous agreement that gave it the option to acquire Cursor, whose engineers have already been working closely with the company",
      "SpaceX is buying a highflying, fast-growing artificial-intelligence startup as it seeks to make its Grok model more competitive.",
      "On Tuesday, as SpaceX’s stock SPCX boomed, the company said it would acquire the parent company of the AI coding startup Cursor for $60 billion. The transaction is expected to close by the end of August, according to the companies."
